{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "ddd217b7-aaec-57ce-bbda-571f4a4ee8e2",
		"name": "NPHIIS Lab API",
		"description": "Everything lab: results the lab system (LIMS) sends to NPHIIS (hie-auth `POST /lab/results`), staff pulling results, and the NPHL submission operations.\n\n## Portal: POST /lab/updates\n\nSame message body as `/lab/results`, but for admin-portal staff (Bearer JWT). Roles: ADMINISTRATOR, SUPERUSER, LAB_TECHNICIAN, NATIONAL_LAB. Creates missing specimen Tasks when needed (`createMissingTasks`). No lab API key or HMAC.\n\n## LIMS: POST /lab/results\n\nOne endpoint takes everything the lab sends about a specimen submitted to NPHL, as an array or `{ \"data\": [...] }`. Each message has `messageType` and the specimen's `specimenIdentifier` (`message_type` / `specimen_id` also work):\n\n| messageType | Effect on the specimen |\n|---|---|\n| `result` (or none) | Preliminary or final result: Observations, DiagnosticReport, Task `preliminary-result` / `final-result`; submitter emailed |\n| `rejected` | Task `specimen-rejected`, Specimen `unsatisfactory`; submitter emailed |\n| `received` | Task `received-at-lab` |\n| `in-testing` | Task `in-testing` |\n| `note` | Note added to the Task |\n\nA specimen is matched on its tube label (the ID it was submitted to NPHL with), then on `orderIdentifier` if sent. Progress never steps back: `received` after `in-testing`, or either after a result or rejection, is ignored. Sending the same message twice changes nothing.\n\n**Auth:** `x-api-key: {{labApiKey}}`. When the server has `LAB_RESULTS_HMAC_SECRET`, set `{{hmacSecret}}` and the collection signs each request (`x-lab-timestamp`, `x-lab-signature`); a timestamp more than 5 minutes off is refused.\n\n| Status | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| 200 | Processed. `results[]`: per update `matched`, `matchedOn`, `status`, `businessStatus`. `invalid[]`: unusable messages by `index` |\n| 400 | No usable message; `invalid[]` says why |\n| 401 | Wrong key, or missing/invalid/stale signature |\n| 503 | `LAB_RESULTS_API_KEY` not configured on the server |\n\nSet `{{specimenId}}` to the tube label of a specimen that has been submitted to NPHL.\n\n## Operations (`/subscriptions/specimens/*`)\nAuth: `X-Internal-Api-Key: {{internalApiKey}}` (`INTERNAL_SUBSCRIPTION_API_KEY`), or a Bearer token of an ADMINISTRATOR / SUPERUSER. Each call is logged in the admin callback log.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "LIMS - POST /lab/results",
			"description": "Calls from the lab system. Auth: `x-api-key: {{labApiKey}}` (or `Authorization: Bearer`). Signed automatically when `{{hmacSecret}}` is set.",
			"auth": {
				"type": "apikey",
				"apikey": [
					{
						"key": "key",
						"value": "x-api-key",
						"type": "string"
					},
					{
						"key": "value",
						"value": "{{labApiKey}}",
						"type": "string"
					},
					{
						"key": "in",
						"value": "header",
						"type": "string"
					}
				]
			},
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "prerequest",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"// Signs the request when hmacSecret is set (the server requires it when LAB_RESULTS_HMAC_SECRET is set):",
							"// x-lab-signature = sha256=<hex HMAC-SHA256 of \"<timestamp>.<raw body>\">.",
							"const secret = pm.collectionVariables.get(\"hmacSecret\");",
							"if (secret && pm.request.body && pm.request.body.raw !== undefined) {",
							"  const ts = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000).toString();",
							"  const body = pm.variables.replaceIn(pm.request.body.raw);",
							"  pm.request.body.raw = body;",
							"  const sig = CryptoJS.HmacSHA256(ts + \".\" + body, secret).toString(CryptoJS.enc.Hex);",
							"  pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: \"x-lab-timestamp\", value: ts });",
							"  pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: \"x-lab-signature\", value: \"sha256=\" + sig });",
							"}"
						]
					}
				}
			],
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Results",
					"item": [
						{
							"name": "Result - lab line-list rows",
							"request": {
								"method": "POST",
								"header": [
									{
										"key": "Content-Type",
										"value": "application/json"
									}
								],
								"url": {
									"raw": "{{API_HOST}}/lab/results",
									"host": [
										"{{API_HOST}}"
									],
									"path": [
										"lab",
										"results"
									]
								},
								"description": "The lab's line-list shape, as lab-staging `GET /list` returns it: one row per test, grouped per specimen. `conclusion` Absent/Present (or Negative/Positive, or LOINC `valueCode` LA9634-2 / LA9633-4). Any positive test makes the specimen positive. Rows carry no preliminary flag, so the result is recorded as final. `caseIdentifier` is kept on the Task as the lab number; `componentCode` is added to the test Observations as LOINC.",
								"body": {
									"mode": "raw",
									"raw": "{\n  \"data\": [\n    {\n      \"subjectIdentifier\": \"NVRL/1051/26\",\n      \"caseIdentifier\": \"NVRL/1051/26\",\n      \"identifier\": \"10175\",\n      \"orderIdentifier\": \"\",\n      \"specimenIdentifier\": \"{{specimenId}}\",\n      \"specimenType\": \"Blood\",\n      \"collectDate\": \"2026-10-14\",\n      \"performerMFL\": \"13080\",\n      \"effectiveDateTime\": \"2026-10-15\",\n      \"code\": \"86518-8\",\n      \"testName\": \"EVD\",\n      \"codeText\": \"Ebola Virus\",\n      \"componentCode\": \"86518-8\",\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"unit\": \"NONE\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"Absent\",\n      \"valueCode\": \"LA9634-2\",\n      \"testingLabCode\": \"20580\",\n      \"testingLabName\": \"National Virology Reference Laboratory (NVRL)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"subjectIdentifier\": \"NVRL/1051/26\",\n      \"caseIdentifier\": \"NVRL/1051/26\",\n      \"identifier\": \"10175\",\n      \"orderIdentifier\": \"\",\n      \"specimenIdentifier\": \"{{specimenId}}\",\n      \"specimenType\": \"Blood\",\n      \"collectDate\": \"2026-10-14\",\n      \"performerMFL\": \"13080\",\n      \"effectiveDateTime\": \"2026-10-15\",\n      \"code\": \"86574-1\",\n      \"testName\": \"MARBUG\",\n      \"codeText\": \"Marburg Virus\",\n      \"componentCode\": \"86574-1\",\n      \"value\": null,\n      \"unit\": \"NONE\",\n      \"conclusion\": \"Absent\",\n      \"valueCode\": \"LA9634-2\",\n      \"testingLabCode\": \"20580\",\n      \"testingLabName\": \"National Virology Reference Laboratory (NVRL)\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
									"options": {
										"raw": {
											"language": "json"
										}
									}
								}
							},
							"response": [],
							"event": [
								{
									"listen": "test",
									"script": {
										"type": "text/javascript",
										"exec": [
											"pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
											"const r = pm.response.json();",
											"pm.test(\"every update matched a submitted specimen\", () => pm.expect(r.results.filter((o) => !o.matched)).to.eql([]));",
											"pm.test(\"final result\", () => pm.expect(r.results[0].businessStatus).to.eql(\"final-result\"));"
										]
									}
								}
							]
						},
